Privacy Policy for Midnight Rig: Neon Haul
Last Updated: November 13, 2026
1. Overview & Information We Do Not Collect
Insight Studios ("we," "our," or "us") built Midnight Rig: Neon Haul as an ad-supported free mobile game. We respect your privacy and do not require user accounts, logins, or registration, and we do not collect or store personal details, phone numbers, contacts, precise GPS location, or hardware serial identifiers on our own servers.
2. Third-Party Advertising (Google AdMob)
To keep Midnight Rig: Neon Haul free to download and play, the game displays third-party advertisements served through Google AdMob (Google Mobile Ads SDK). These third-party ads appear in two ways:
Optional Rewarded Ads: Players may choose to watch a sponsored video ad in exchange for in-game benefits (such as Emergency Roadside Repair, Emergency Fuel Dispatch, Overtime Extension, Waiving a DOT Inspection Delay, or a 2× Contract Payout Bonus).
Interstitial Ads: Occasional full-screen transition ads may be shown between completed delivery contracts.
When you use the app, Google AdMob and Google Play Services may automatically collect and process certain data in accordance with Google’s privacy practices, including:
Device & Technical Specifications: Device model, manufacturer, operating system version, screen resolution, system language, and network/carrier type.
Advertising & Device Identifiers: Android Advertising ID (AAID) and app-set identifiers used for ad delivery, frequency capping, attribution, and fraud prevention.
Approximate Location: General region/country derived from your IP address (not precise GPS).
Ad Interaction & Diagnostic Data: Ad impressions, view duration, click-throughs, rewarded-ad completion events, and SDK crash/performance diagnostics.
Where required by regional law (such as in the EEA or UK), the app uses Google’s User Messaging Platform (UMP) consent dialog so you can manage your ad-personalization preferences.
This third-party service processes data in accordance with its own privacy policy:
Google Play Services & Google AdMob: https://policies.google.com/privacy
How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites
3. Device Permissions Used
Midnight Rig: Neon Haul requests only the minimum device permissions required for gameplay and third-party ad delivery:
android.permission.VIBRATE: Triggers tactile haptic feedback when shifting gears, stomping the pneumatic air brake, or colliding with curbs.
android.permission.WAKE_LOCK: Keeps the phone display illuminated while actively maneuvering and driving the truck, preventing unwanted screen dimming during gameplay.
android.permission.INTERNET & android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE: Required to load and display third-party Google AdMob ad inventory (rewarded videos and interstitials) and verify network connectivity.
com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID: Used by the Google Mobile Ads (AdMob) SDK to access the Android Advertising ID for ad serving, measurement, and anti-fraud checks.
4. Local Data Storage (Career Stats & Preferences)
All game progress and player preferences are stored strictly locally on your device (via HTML5 localStorage / WebView app storage), including:
Unlocked contract tiers and route completions
Career Stats: Anonymous local driver slots (Driver Slot 1–3), any optional arcade callsign you type in, lifetime mileage, deliveries completed, accidents avoided, clean haul streaks, and best parking grades
Driving preferences (Control Stick / touch layout: Centered, Split, Left, or Right) and audio mute/volume settings
This local data is never transmitted to our servers or tracked off-device. You can erase your Career Stats at any time using the in-game Reset Stats option, or remove all local data by clearing the app’s storage/cache or uninstalling the game.
5. Children’s Privacy (COPPA Compliance)
Midnight Rig: Neon Haul is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from children under 13.
If you are a parent or guardian and believe that your child has provided personal information or that an integrated ad provider has inadvertently collected data from a child under 13, please contact us immediately at contact@df.services, and we will take prompt steps to assist and address the issue.
6. Your Rights and Opting Out of Targeted Advertising
You have control over how advertising data is used on your Android device:
Reset or Delete Advertising ID: Open your Android device’s Settings → Google → Ads (or Privacy → Ads depending on Android version), where you can reset your Advertising ID or select "Delete advertising ID" / opt out of ad personalization across apps.
GDPR / UK GDPR / CCPA / CPRA Notice: If you reside in the European Economic Area (EEA), the United Kingdom, or California, you have rights regarding access, correction, restriction, or deletion of personal data processed by third-party ad networks. You can manage consent via the in-app consent prompt (where applicable) or exercise your rights through Google’s privacy portal linked in Section 2. Because Insight Studios does not store personal profiles on its own servers, we hold no personal data about you.
7. Security
We take the security of your device seriously. Midnight Rig: Neon Haul operates strictly within the standard Android application sandbox, and all network transmissions initiated by the third-party Google AdMob SDK are encrypted in transit via Transport Layer Security (HTTPS/TLS).
